\section{Discussion and Conclusion}\label{sec:discussion}\label{sec:selection_method}\label{sec:conclusion}

Degeneracy ($12$--$68$\%) limits diversity while signal alignment collapse ($\alpha{\to}0$) limits ranking. Our decomposition (\S\ref{sec:theory}) identifies $\alpha$ as the binding constraint ($8$--$33{\times}$ tighter): high degeneracy rules out SC benefit; low degeneracy with LP-F1 alignment may warrant entity construction; otherwise, greedy remains optimal.
